what:
observe, addendum to 01405 (Andrew, 17:49): flake apps for Tracy beside apps.blaze. `nix run .#tracy` on macOS and Linux opens the viewer, ready to connect to a blaze built with --features tracy.

1. nix/tracy.nix: copy docs/v2/plan/lanes/observe/tracy.nix (in the tree; it supersedes the /tmp/tracy-nix/tracy.nix named in 01405). It is Tracy v0.14.1, the exact version the fork's client speaks (tracing-tracy 0.12.0 / tracy-client-sys 0.30.0), with the source pinned by hash: fetchFromGitHub wolfpld/tracy rev v0.14.1, sha256-vcLI9jb7eYcR162LgBQ2P4A0oiZuYRfYRQiDhlAk5TI=. Its CPM sources are pinned by hash too. Our nixpkgs (e513db7b) only has tracy_0_13 = 0.13.1, so the file overrides that package's src rather than using it. Since 01405 one thing changed: on Linux the file now builds the X11/GLFW viewer (withWayland = false, Tracy's LEGACY, plus libx11), because nixpkgs' default Wayland-only viewer does not open on an X11 desktop; X11 also runs under Wayland through XWayland. On macOS that changes nothing. Built and run on aarch64-darwin before this change (/nix/store/3ckii861nny2asabf41xwv73ia77z6bc-tracy-0.14.1, tracy-capture and tracy-csvexport print 0.14.1). Linux is unbuilt: please build `.#tracy` on x86_64-linux and aarch64-linux. If find_package(X11) or GL fails there, those are the inputs to look at.

2. flake.nix, in the `let` (next to `run`/`life`):
        # Tracy v0.14.1, the version the client of blaze's feature `tracy` speaks (tracing-tracy
        # 0.12.0; other versions refuse to connect): the viewer, tracy-capture and tracy-csvexport
        # (docs/profiling.md).
        tracy = import ./nix/tracy.nix { inherit pkgs; };
   in packages: `inherit tracy;`
   and beside apps.blaze:
        # `nix run .#tracy`: Tracy's viewer, to connect to a blaze built with `--features tracy`.
        apps.tracy = {
          type = "app";
          program = "${tracy}/bin/tracy";
        };
        apps.tracy-capture = {
          type = "app";
          program = "${tracy}/bin/tracy-capture";
        };
        apps.tracy-csvexport = {
          type = "app";
          program = "${tracy}/bin/tracy-csvexport";
        };
   and `tracy` in devShells.default's packages (01405 item 1).

3. docs/profiling.md now leads with `nix run .#tracy` (draft: docs/v2/plan/lanes/observe/profiling.md, moved as 01405 item 2 says). One caveat it states: on a non-NixOS Linux the viewer needs the host's OpenGL driver (nixGL); `nix run` cannot fix that from inside the flake.

Check: `nix run .#tracy` opens the viewer on the Mac; `nix run .#tracy-capture -- -h` and `nix run .#tracy-csvexport -- -h` print 0.14.1; `nix flake check`.
